-- Real Tier 1 content for Topics I.II through I.V (Topic I.I was loaded separately).
-- Same pattern as the first content migration: fixed UUIDs for topic/subtopic
-- rows (safe to re-run), slides/questions are a single-shot load.
--
-- Two content-mapping decisions, flagged for review:
-- 1. True/false questions are stored as question_type = 'mcq' with
--    options ["True","False"] -- there's no dedicated true_false UI component,
--    and a T/F question is just a 2-option MCQ, so this reuses the existing,
--    tested renderer rather than adding a new one for 6 questions.
-- 2. The one "put these in order" question (I.III.I) is stored as a 4-option
--    MCQ describing possible orderings, per instruction, since drag-to-reorder
--    wasn't worth building for a single question.

